QuestGuidance.Register("en",294,{
[9377]="70009F58\n1\tTalk to Anlaf the Forlorn at The Forsaken Inn\tAnlaf is in The Forsaken Inn, located in the Lone-lands along the Great East Road, between Bree and Ost Guruth. Hana the Young has asked you to inquire at The Forsaken Inn about acquiring a shipment of oatmeal for Ost Guruth.\n2\tTalk to Nod Gardener in Oatbarton\tThe Bounder Nod Gardener lives in Oatbarton on the border of the Shire, north of Brockenborings and across the Greenfields. Anlaf the Forlorn of The Forsaken Inn has asked you to journey to Oatbarton to talk to Old Mugwort's cousin Nod Gardener. He has heard that there are problems on the northern boundary of the Shire that the Bounders have not been able to solve, and that shipments of oatmeal will not be possible until the trouble in Oatbarton has been resolved.\n",
[9378]="70009973\n1\tCollect oats (total: 12)\tNibs Chubb's fields are east and north-east of his farm. Nibs Chubb has asked you to help him collect his oats from the fields.\n2\tTalk to Nibs Chubb\030Collect Oats (total: 12)\tNibs Chubb is at his farm, in the south of Oatbarton. You should return to Nibs Chubb with the oats.\n",
[9379]="700529EC\n1\tDefeat goblins in Waldfast (total: 10)\tGoblins have taken over the village of Waldfast in southern Wolf-denes. You should defeat goblins in Waldfast.\n2\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár. If Langhár is no longer with you, she may be outside Waldfast or in Vegbár.\n",
[9380]="70028FAE\n1\tTalk to Garrun to journey into the cavern below Cuvnerth\tGarrun is at his camp, west of Cuvnerth. You should speak with Garrun when you are ready to enter Cuvnerth.\n2\tTalk to Garrun in the Isendale\tGarrun is at his encampment, west of Cuvnerth. You should speak with Garrun regarding your discoveries in the cavern.\n",
[9381]="7000B2BC\n1\tTalk to Greylond Bottomley at the Mathom House\tGreylond Bottomley can be found outside the Mathom House in Michel Delving. Hithlim has asked that you speak with Greylond Bottomley to find out what the Mathom Society is up to.\n",
[9382]="7005A68F\n1\tHalvar has asked you to retrieve some dried meat from a rations crate, but he's not sure which one. The crates can be found around Ashmargathâl.\t\n2\tTalk to Halvar\tYou should deliver the dried meats to Halvar, who's waiting by one of the camp-fires in Ashmargathâl.\n3\tAsk Dági for beer\tDági can be found somewhere in Ashmargathâl. To complete the dish, Halvar would like for you to ask Dági for some beer.\n4\tTalk to Halvar\tHalvar is waiting by one of the camp-fires in Ashmargathâl. You should bring the beer to him.\n",
[9383]="7002A7E6\n1\tTravel with Dagoras to defend Quickbeam's grove\tDagoras is at his camp near Isengard. Dagoras asked you to accompany the Grimbold's emissary to the gates of Isengard. You should speak with Dagoras when you are ready to meet the emissary.\n2\tSpeak with Quickbeam\tDagoras is at his camp near Isengard. You should tell Dagoras what transpired at the meeting between Ordwaer and Saruman before the gates of Isengard.\n",
[9384]="70052963\n1\tTravel to the Forest Gate\tThe Forest Gate can be found at the eastern edge of the Beorning-lands where the Vale of Anduin meets Eryn Lasgalen. You should travel to the Forest Gate and tell the Wood-elves of Grimbeorn's decision.\n2\tTell Legolas of Grimbeorn's decision\tLegolas can be found at the Forest Gate at the eastern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should tell Legolas of Grimbeorn's decision.\n3\tDefeat enemies in Eryn Lasgalen (total: 10)\tWild beasts and enemies, such as fire-flies, huorns, Orcs, spiders, Taurogrim, and wolves, can still be found in Eryn Lasgalen. You should defeat enemies in Eryn Lasgalen to make the roads safer.\n4\tTalk to Legolas at the Beorninghús\tLegolas can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[9385]="7006615A\n1\tTalk to Myldil\tCalpheth has asked you to search near Lothgobel for signs of her wayward father, Myldil. Lothgobel is in northern Lamedon.\n2\tCollect clay (total: 8)\030Collect quartz crystals (total: 6)\tMyldil has suggested that your time would be well spent digging up clay and gathering quartz crystals. Clay can be found along the banks of the streams that flow about Tathrendalf. Quartz can be found on the cliff walls north of Tathrendalf.\n3\tReturn to Myldil\tYou have gathered wet clay and sparkling quartz for Myldil. You should bring them to him in Lothgobel. Lothgobel is in Lamedon.\n",
[9386]="7004D70E\n1\tTalk to Tárasánë, the Green Lady\tTárasánë, the Green Lady, can be found in the ruins of Caras Tilion. The Green Lady desires to learn your intentions in seeking an audience with her.\n2\tTalk to Tárasánë, the Green Lady\tTárasánë, the Green Lady, can be found in the ruins of Caras Tilion. You have experienced a great vision brought on by the Green Lady.\n3\tTalk to King Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You have witnessed the power of the Green Lady and should now return to King Thranduil.\n",
[9387]="7000EE2B\n1\tDefend Juhani\tJuhani, reported missing by his friend Tero back in Zigilgund, is trapped on the isle of Kissa-sari. He wishes your help in ensuring him safe passage.\n2\tTalk to Tero in Zigilgund\tYou have escorted Juhani to safety. You should tell Tero that he is now safe.\n",
[9388]="70066A6F\n1\tSearch for Dorach\tAndrethil is frantic with worry over her missing child, Dorach, who she think may have gone to the nearby island to challenge its fierce dread-turtles. You should head to Loeg Thangalf and look for Dorach.\n2\tTalk to Dorach\tWhile searching Loeg Thangalf you managed to find Dorach, who is eager to speak with you. Loeg Thangalf is in northern Pinnath Gelin.\n3\tSearch for Dorach's sword\tYou rescued Dorach, but she's worried about the sword she dropped on the north-eastern part of the Loeg Thangalf. You should retrieve the sword and return it to her.\n4\tBring the sword to Dorach\tOn Loeg Thangalf you found a small sword that had been dropped by Dorach. You should bring the sword to Dorach at Mereham, in central Pinnath Gelin.\n5\tTalk to Andrethil\tYou have returned Thumb-cleaver to Dorach, and her mother, Andrethil is waiting now to speak with you. Andrethil is at Mereham in central Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[9389]="70015E30\n1\tDefeat frost-grims (total: 8)\030Defeat snow-beasts (total: 8)\tFrost-grims and snow-beasts have been seen in the Redhorn Gate, north-east of Echad Dúnann. Rostoriel has asked you to quell the rage of Caradhras and defeat the beasts that dwell within the Redhorn Gate.\n2\tTalk to Rostoriel at Echad Dúnann\tRostoriel is at Echad Dúnann, south-west of the Redhorn Gate and east of the Burnt Tor. You should return to Rostoriel and tell her of your success.\n",
[9390]="7000ACA2\n1\tPresent 'Of Mysteries Most Profound' to Cachúnir in Rivendell\030Craft 'Of Mysteries Most Profound' (quantity: see journal)\tCachúnir is at Rivendell, in the Trollshaws. Cachúnir has asked you to pen an essay entitled 'Of Mysteries Most Profound' and bring it to him.\n",
[9391]="70049569\n1\tThe strangers can be found to the south of Spakorth at the foot of the statue of Sauron outside the Oath-taker's Horn. Spakorth has spotted two strangers at the foot of the nearby statue of Sauron and desires to learn their purpose in Mordor.\t\n2\tTalk to Megoril\tThe two Elves, Megoril and Dernaith, can be found at the foot of the statue of Sauron outside the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth. You have come across a pair of Elves searching the ruins of Dor Amarth.\n",
[9392]="700658F1\n1\tCollect fuingil (total: 6)\030Collect lethelin (total: 10)\tAtharon has asked you to gather ingredients for potion making while you are searching the forest. Fuingil and lethelin can be found in the forest and caves west of Imloth Melui.\n2\tReturn to Atharon\tYou should bring the plants and mushrooms to Atharon. Atharon is in the Hall of the Gentle Hand in Imloth Melui.\n",
[9393]="70050E1E\n1\tSearch around for the Ungoledain that left these weapons behind\tUngoladan-weapons litter the landscape nearby. It is doubtful they were left behind intentionally.\n2\tSearch around for the Ungoledain that left these weapons behind\tUngoladan-weapons litter the landscape nearby. It is doubtful they were purposely left behind.\n3\tCompleted\tUngoladan-weapons litter the landscape nearby. It is doubtful they were purposely left behind.\n",
[9394]="70065B00\n1\tTalk to Halgúr\tSadrien has asked you to deliver a message to Halgúr at his homestead south of Imloth Melui.\n2\tExamine the rubble\tHalgúr is ignoring you. Perhaps you can learn more by searching his homestead.\n3\tInvestigate the food stores\tThe homestead looks to have been ransacked.\n4\tCheck on Halgúr's supplies\tAll the edible food has been taken. The rest has been left to rot.\n5\tInvestigate Halgúr's materials\tThe supplies have not seen much use. Halgúr seems to be working aimlessly.\n6\tExamine the ruins\tThe materials have been destroyed. They will not see any use.\n7\tTalk to Halgúr\tPart of Halgúr's homestead has collapsed. Something terrible must have happened. Speak to Halgúr.\n8\tTalk to Sadrien\tHalgúr does not wish to speak to you anymore. Perhaps Sadrien in Imloth Melui has more information on what transpired at the homestead.\n9\tInvestigate Melnith's retreat\tSadrien asks you to find Melnith's retreat east of Imloth Melui.\n10\tTalk to Halgúr\tInform Halgúr of Melnith's retreat. Halgúr can be found at his homestead south of Imloth Melui.\n11\tBeckon Halgúr (total: 3)\tHalgúr is still not willing to listen. He needs to be encouraged in some way.\n12\tTalk to Halgúr\tYou have convinced Halgúr to meet you at Melnith's retreat.\n13\tTalk to Sadrien\tHalgúr has a renewed sense of hope for the world. Inform Sadrien back in Imloth Melui.\n",
[9395]="70061F83\n1\tTalk to Gurthern\tGurthern will meet you where he last saw the elhudan to search for the missing child. He waits for you by a pond in Tyrn Gorthad. You should speak with Gurthern.\n2\tSearch for the missing child\030Speak to the wailing woman\tGurthern believes that the missing child may have followed one of the elhudan, the glowing wisp-like orbs, into the wilderness of Tyrn Gorthad. You should look for the elhudan that Gurthern saw around this area.\n3\tReturn to Gurthern\tAfter following the elhudan, you found the missing child unharmed. The wailing woman fled up the hill, while the child fled towards Gurthern. You should return to Gurthern and share what you found.\n",
[9396]="7001750A\n1\tTalk to Kaldi at the entrance to the Vile Maw\tKaldi should be in the Vile Maw, west and a little north of the Great Wheel. Foreman Indrith fears that he may have sent his worker and friend Kaldi to his death. He has sent you to a camp where he believes Kaldi should be.\n",
[9397]="700173BC\n1\tDefeat General Talug\tFil Gashan lies to the south-west of Anazârmekhem. Yngvi has asked you to enter Fil Gashan and defeat General Talug. He suggested that heating the General's armour may make him more vulnerable to attack.\n2\tTalk to Yngvi at Anazârmekhem\tYngvi is at Anazârmekhem, north-east of Fil Gashan. You found a way to defeat General Talug and turned his forces against him. With the general defeated, it is possible that Mazog and his army will be slowed to a crawl. You should return to Yngvi and tell him this news.\n",
[9398]="70032BF2\n1\tBurn Durub shrines (total: 2)\tThe Durub shrine is in the camp of Gazatu-ru, south of the Twenty-first Hall. Dómárr has asked you to burn shrines in Gazatu-ru Durub Orc-camp.\n2\tReturn to Dómárr\tDómárr is at his encampment in the Great Hall of Durin. You should return to Dómárr.\n",
[9399]="70017595\n1\tTalk to Sadreda at the Shadowed Refuge\030Defeat the Dark Warden and collect its head\tThe Dark Warden, if it exists, dwells somewhere within the Foundations of Stone in Moria, far to the east and south of the Lone-lands. Mosco Mudbottom has tasked you with discovering the lair of the Dark Warden and bringing the creature's head to Sadreda.\n",
[9400]="7003A40C\n1\tThere are many shop owners in Woodhurst. Gifemund has asked you to speak with the healer, supplier, provisioner, and the innkeeper on his behalf.\t\n2\tTalk to Herubrand\tHerubrand is in the cellar of the farm-house. Herubrand would be interested to hear of the offer being made by Gifemund to the merchants of Woodhurst.\n3\tTalk to Gifemund\tGifemund awaits your return in the ore refinery. Gifemund will be interested to hear the answers to his offer.\n",
[9401]="7006EC45\n1\tTalk to the thirsty beachgoer\tThere appears to be someone in need of help on the small beach beside the harbour.\n2\tFind a refreshing beverage inside The Cracked Flagon\tThe thirsty beachgoer has asked you to get a drink from inside The Cracked Flagon.\n3\tBring the refreshing beverage to the thirsty beachgoer\tYou have gotten a refreshing beverage from inside The Cracked Flagon. You should bring it to the thirsty beachgoer on the small beach near the harbour.\n4\tTalk to the relaxing holidayer\tThere may be someone else in the harbour area that needs help.\n5\tFind the relaxing holidayer's book\tThe relaxing holidayer has asked you to go into her room in The Cracked Flagon to find her book and bring it to her.\n6\tBring the relaxing holidayer her book\tYou have found the relaxing holidayer's book, \"A Memory of Mûmakil\". You should bring it to her at her bench in the harbour area.\n7\tTalk to the unsettled sightseer\tThere may be someone on the southern beach that needs help.\n8\tFind a cushion for the unsettled sightseer\tThe unsettled sightseer has asked you for a cushion to sit on. The Cracked Flagon probably has something.\n9\tBring the cushion to the unsettled sightseer\tYou have found a cushion for the unsettled sightseer. You should bring it to him on the southern beach.\n10\tTalk to the hopeful suitor\tThere appears to be someone else on the southern beach who needs help. You should talk to them.\n11\tFind a picnic basket\tThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You should head back to The Cracked Flagon and see what you can find.\n12\tBring the empty basket to the cook, Sâghlem\tThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You have a basket, now you must fill it. Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon can probably help you.\n13\tPick up the filled basket\tThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You brought an empty basket to Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon, who filled it for you.\n14\tBring the filled picnic basket to the hopeful suitor\tThe hopeful suitor has requested a picnic basket of food. You brought an empty basket to Sâghlem, the cook at The Cracked Flagon, who filled it for you. You should bring the filled basket to the hopeful suitor on the southern beach.\n15\tTalk to the queer merrymaker\tIt seems there is another person on the southern beach who needs help. You should talk to them.\n16\tBury the queer merrymaker in the sand\tThe queer merrymaker has requested that you bury him in the sand.\n17\tBury the queer merrymaker some more\tThe queer merrymaker has requested that you bury him in the sand even more than you already have.\n18\tTalk to Merkhâma\tYou have buried the queer merrymaker in the sand and don't see anyone else in need of help. You should return to Merkhâma outside of The Cracked Flagon to get your reward.\n",
[9402]="7006B5FD\n1\tHunt deer and collect venison (total: 6)\tThe destructive Ikorbâni harts and hinds can be found in the rice fields of Ekagar in Ambarûl.\n2\tBring the venison to Urama\tYou have hunted deer and collected venison. You should bring the meat to Urama.\n",
[9403]="70070CFC\n1\tDestroy rat nests (total: 4)\030Defeat rats in Sul Madásh (total: 15)\tYour mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in number and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.\n2\tDefeat the monstrous rat\tYour mission is to rid Sul Madásh of its rat problem. They are growing in number and becoming a problem for the settlement. The rats must be stopped and their nests destroyed.\n",
[9404]="7000AC5A\n1\tDeliver the oil to Soldier Gozad at Tírith Rhaw\030Collect Barrel of Oil (total: 5)\tThe Free Peoples carry barrels of oil that can be used to fill the iron pots being built at Tírith Rhaw. Seek out the Free People guarding locations throughout the Ettenmoors and slaughter them for the oil they carry. The War-tyrant desires to use boiling oil at Tírith Rhaw to punish the enemy as they make their assault. You were sent into the Ettenmoors to collect oil from the foe.\n",
[9405]="7000AC59\n1\tDeliver the oil to Soldier Kaafaz at Lugazag\030Collect Barrel of Oil (total: 5)\tThe Free Peoples carry barrels of oil that can be used to fill the iron pots being built at Lugazag. Seek out the Free People guarding locations throughout the Ettenmoors and slaughter them for the oil they carry. The War-tyrant desires to use boiling oil at Lugazag to punish the enemy as they make their assault. You were sent into the Ettenmoors to collect barrels of oil from the foe.\n",
[9406]="7000AE19\n1\tDeliver the barrels of oil to Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect barrels of oil (total: 5)\tOrcs and Uruks guarding fortifications and found patrolling the wild of the Ettenmoors may carry barrels of oil. Sergeant-at-Arms Gautr at Tol Ascarnen is working to forge an iron cauldron to fill with oil to be used against the forces of Angmar as they try to retake the keep from the Free Peoples. He has asked you to collect the oil from the Enemy.\n",
[9407]="7000AE32\n1\tDeliver the oil to Sergeant-at-Arms Kolr at Lugazag\030Collect barrels of oil (total: 5)\tEnemies throughout the Ettenmoors carry stolen barrels of oil. Sergeant-at-Arms Kolr received orders to forge a great iron cauldron to fill with oil. This cauldron will be used to defend the walls of Lugazag from the Enemy. He has asked you to recover the stolen barrels of oil which are in the possession of the Enemy.\n",
[9408]="7000AE33\n1\tDeliver the oil to Sergeant-at-Arms Haliggyr at Tírith Rhaw\030Collect barrels of oil (total: 5)\tFoes throughout the Ettenmoors carry barrels of oil, stolen from the stores of the Free Peoples. Sergeant-at-Arms Haliggyr received orders to forge a great iron cauldron to fill with oil. This cauldron will be used to defend the walls of Tírith Rhaw from the Enemy. He tasked you with recovering as much oil as you can from the servants of the Enemy.\n",
})
